# Skan project-owned IPv4 active OS fingerprint corpus.
# Clean-room signatures derived from common TCP/IP stack behavior only.
# These profiles intentionally describe stack "styles" rather than claiming that
# a few packet fields uniquely identify a precise OS release or distribution.
# TTL ranges account for ordinary routed-hop decrement from common initial values.

# Modern Linux server/client style: 64-ish TTL, large initial receive window,
# SACK+timestamps, and Linux-like SYN/SYN-ACK option ordering.
Fingerprint LinuxModern64240
ID=skan-v4-linux-modern-64240
SPECIFICITY=18
ADDRESS_FAMILY=IPv4
Class Linux | Linux kernel | modern | general-purpose
TTL_RANGE=45-64
DF=Y
WINDOW=64240
MSS=1460
WSCALE=7
SACK=Y
TIMESTAMP=Y
TCP_OPTIONS=MSS,SACK,TS,NOP,WS
RESPONSE_BEHAVIOR=SYN_ACK
RESPONSE_PRESENCE=YES
ICMP_TTL_RANGE=45-64

